# =============================================================================
#  Runtime state and secrets - never commit these.
#  Everything the stack produces while running lands in state/.
# =============================================================================

# --- runtime state -----------------------------------------------------------
state/
*.log
!docs/**/*.log

# SmartDNS runtime artefacts
/smartdns.cache
# (removed: the audit CSV is kept under archive/smartdns/ and must not be ignored)
/smartdns.console.log
status.json
hotspot-status.json
autolearn.json
autolearn-summary.json
adapter-monitor.json
adapter-monitor.log

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The Aliyun host credentials and the shadowsocks key live outside the repo,
# but guard against an accidental copy.
*credential*
*password*
*secret*
aliyun-server.txt
hysteria2.json
ss-key.txt
known_hosts
*.pem
*.key
!config/*.key.example

# --- backups / one-off artefacts ---------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.tmp
*.disabled
*.permigrate
*-backup.txt
tmp-*.conf
proxyoverride-backup.txt
sysproxy-backup-before-mihomo.txt

# --- runtime/ : the deployed mihomo install ----------------------------------
# Source that lives in here (mihomo-supervisor.ps1) IS versioned. Everything the
# install ships or the run produces is not:
#   * mihomo.exe is 61 MB and GeoSite.dat another 4 MB - not repository content;
#   * config.yaml is excluded ON PURPOSE. The live file carries the shadowsocks
#     and hysteria2 passwords, and this repo's rule is that secrets are never
#     committed. The cost is that the hand-written half of that config (DNS
#     policy, rules, group order) is not versioned either; see README.
runtime/mihomo.exe
runtime/*.exe
runtime/*.dat
runtime/cache.db
runtime/mihomo.err
runtime/*.log.old
runtime/config.yaml
runtime/config.yaml.*
# The switch's own artefacts: `-DryRun` writes config.hypomux-dryrun.yaml beside
# the live config (mihomo resolves ./providers relative to it), and a backup taken
# by hand gets a suffix. Both carry the live secrets, so both stay out of git.
runtime/config.hypomux-*.yaml
runtime/config.yaml.pre-*
runtime/providers/
runtime/rules/
# Archived standalone sing-box capture experiment. Current egress capture is
# owned by HypoMux's separately installed TUN/engine, not these local binaries.
runtime/sing-box/
# The dashboard mihomo serves at /ui/ is a 2.5 MB vendored download, not repo
# content: fetch or update it with tools\Install-Metacubexd.ps1.
runtime/ui/
runtime/ui.staging/

# --- OS / editor -------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# --- PowerShell --------------------------------------------------------------
# Module analysis cache
*.psd1.bak
testResults.xml

# TUN driver: a third-party binary, copied in beside mihomo.exe (see docs).
# Required by tun: and deliberately not vendored in this repository.
/runtime/wintun.dll

# --- Upstream source reference ------------------------------------------------
# mihomo-src/ is a full clone of MetaCubeX/mihomo kept for reading source and
# local builds. It is not repository content: the clone has its own .git and
# tags (release/v1.19.32 tracks the binary in runtime/, Alpha is upstream dev).
# Never commit it here and never nest it into this repo.
/mihomo-src/

# --- Sub-project: OpenMPTCProuter_test ---------------------------------------
# Moved in 2026-10-20 from Documents\ChatGPT\ as the stack's OMR sub-project:
# it owns the `omr` outbound relay (127.0.0.1:65080), the LAN PAC server
# (:8080) and the OMR VMware VM. 2.4 GB with its own .git - same rule as
# mihomo-src/: placed here, never committed, never nested into this repo.
/OpenMPTCProuter_test/

# Repository-local development dependencies and generated validation output.
/.tools/
/artifacts/
/source-manifest.json
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
